This is a real product defect. The fix is to avoid full re-rendering of the list when only the completed state of an item changes. Instead of replacing the entire innerHTML, we should update only the specific items that changed.

However, looking at the current architecture, the simplest fix that addresses the core issue is to not replace the entire list when toggling individual items. Instead, we can update the specific item's DOM in place.

